+# TLS Backend
+
+This project's current recorded decision is to use rustls as the TLS backend, replacing an earlier selection of OpenSSL; rustls was adopted for its pure-Rust, memory-safe implementation, which avoids the classes of memory-safety vulnerabilities associated with C-based TLS libraries like OpenSSL.
